{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/204794-questions-on-changeling-governnance","id":204794,"title":"Questions on Changeling governnance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-22T01:43:49-07:00","id":204794,"title":"Questions on Changeling governnance","content":"So, if I understand correctly, the way a freehold is governed is that it is passed between the courts of Spring, Summer, Autumn and Winter every season, and the King of those courts is in control for that season and then relinquishes it, yes?<br /> <br /> But if that is the case, then what is the role of the other courts eg Directional (North, South, East, West) and Diurnal (Sun, Moon, Dawn, Dusk)? Do they ever get a say in governance? What is the point of joining one of these courts if it will never be in power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3534-sharonhorste","name":"Sharonhorste","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T01:56:25-07:00","id":204810,"title":"","content":"Typically, freeholds are governed by a single set of courts. You won't often find the Seasonal and Directional courts among the same Changeling population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T02:52:15-07:00","id":204830,"title":"","content":"Hm. Dusk and Dawn are a bit different, as Dusk at least is presented as a Court existing within the Seasonal Court system, and co-existing with Dawn.<br /> <br /> There are other reasons to join Courts besides holding political dominance - because you're drawn to the same emotion as the Court is, or because you find their philosophy appealing, or because you think they're doing necessary work, or you feel they represent you better (see also why people join political parties with no hope of getting into power).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T09:52:31-07:00","id":205080,"title":"","content":"Lords of Summer also off-handedly mentions the Chinese &quot;Four Luck&quot; Freeholds, where the monarchs of a Directional and Seasonal court are wed and share power. The only one I remember at the moment is The Autumn and Western Courts both rule during Fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T22:16:50-07:00","id":205705,"title":"","content":"The Courts have a default succession for the crown, but it seems to ultimately vary by freehold. Miami's crown is hardly moving with the seasons after all, and Hollywood's goes up for auction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T22:36:47-07:00","id":205732,"title":"","content":"It was said above, but generally the different types of court, (Seasonal, Directional, Solar) don't play ball in the same town. As for how rulership gets passed, well that is up to you. I mean, if you really wanted to have them all in one region, it would make for an interesting game of power politics and invasion where the Fae take the back seat (for once).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T22:38:21-07:00","id":220759,"title":"","content":"I'm co-STing the Changeling venue for a game set in Las Vegas where the main freehold covers the city as a whole and is run by the Seasonal Courts, but the Strip is a separate fiefdom that is manned by the Sun and Moon courts and has its own rules depending on the time of day that you're there. The Sun and Moon Monarchs are kind of a second-tier council to the freehold, filling in duties as needed and basically acting as the Jokers to the Royal Cards (King, Queen, Ace and Jack) of the Seasonal Courts. Has worked pretty well so far.<br /> <br /> Also worked up a rather convoluted New York-based set-up where all three court groups were present, with the Seasonal Monarchs acting as the &quot;proper&quot; royals, the Directional Monarchs as the dukes that the barons who divided up the boroughs reported to and the Diurnals acting as the justicars and the keepers of the piece. Never really got to test that one, but it was fun to work the kinks out for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}